he awards Rochford  district councils former chairman  councillor june Lumley said everyone who  was nominated for an award is a winner  the Citizen of the Year awards are the  perfect way to pay tribute to all the  people who make such a difference to  their communities during my year as  chairman I have had both the privilege  and the pleasure of visiting a huge  number of local community and voluntary  groups and I'm humbled and amazed by the  work these people do the talent that  they have and the generosity they show  to others across the district I would  like to thank all those who took the  time to complete nomination forms and  who brought the hard work dedication and  commitment of these people to our  attention at the council our vision is  to make the district  place that provides opportunities for  the best possible quality of life for  all who live work and visit here all of  the winners and nominations this year  represent and support that vision I hope  that by celebrating and recognizing  those who are making such a difference  to our district that it will encourage  them and give further opportunities so  that they can continue making such a  positive difference to their communities  sing-along Greece at Rochford District  Council's open-air cinema grab a blanket  pack a picnic and get down to swain park  on Saturday August the 15th for the  latest in the open air cinema events now  is the chance to sing along to grease  the musical movie age rating PG and  enjoy the great outdoors these evening  events hosted by essex outdoor cinema  have already taken place at hockley  woods and offer everyone the chance of a  great night out at some of the most  impressive surroundings in the district  a bar and food outlet will open to offer  those who require refreshments the  chance to eat and enjoy a true cinematic  experience with the difference Rockford  District Council's portfolio holder for  the community counselor June Lumley said  this is al fresco dining and  entertainment at its best and shows just  how diverse Rochford is both in terms of  the environments we have at our  fingertips and the array of artistic  endeavors we encourage Greece is a  classic of its kind which in the height  of the Great British summer is a must  for family and friends alike let's just  hope the greased lightning appears only  on the big screen please note that open  air cinema venues are subject to  capacity restrictions and entrance  without a pre-booked ticket is not  guaranteed please pre booked your ticket  and avoid arrive early to avoid  disappointment tickets for all showings  are 12 pounds and the gates open at  seven pm and for up-to-date information  and to book  your tickets visit w WX outdoor cinema  com renters rights greater protection  from rogue landlords and letting agents  rochford and rayleigh Citizens Advice  Bureau is participating in a national  campaign to improve standards in the  private rented sector in the last year  more than 80,000 people came to Citizens  Advice nationally suffering problems  with their privately rented homes which  represents a six percent increase on the  previous year our clients are mostly  commonly hit with issues caused by rogue  landlords or letting agents we are  campaigning to put an end to the  following problems for private renters  both locally and nationally which cause  undue strain on thousands of people each  year bad behavior by a landlord or  letting agent such as renting out poorly  maintained properties failing to make  repairs or harassing tenants inflated  fees charged by letting agents for basic  services misleading advertisements by a  landlord or letting agent eviction at  short notice so far this year Citizens  Advice has successfully campaigned to  stop retaliatory eviction of tenants who  complain about poorly maintained  properties and we would like to continue  to build upon this achievement  throughout 2015 if you are currently  experiencing problems caused by a  landlord or letting agent and would like  free independent impartial and  confidential advice please contact  Rochford and rayleigh Citizens Advice  Bureau Rochford office is in back lane  Rochford SS 41 a why opening hours  tuesdays and thursdays from ten a.m. to  2pm the rayleigh office is  situated in the Civic sweet hockley road  rayleigh SS 680 be opening hours are  mondays thursdays and fridays from ten  a.m. to 2pm you can telephone 03 double  44 double 70 80 8 monday to friday  between 10am and 4pm you can email w WH  foods cabg OG UK online advice including  web chat monday to friday 9am to 5pm  www.vitac.com unity messaging ECM  enables everyone in essex to receive and  share the very latest information about  crime and community safety in their  local area everyone who registers for  ECM will receive accurate and up-to-date  information crime prevention advice and  notifications from essex police officers  essex watch liaison officers and other  key partners such as neighborhood watch  about crime and community safety issues  in their local area you can register at  ww essex community messaging dot org  users will be able to select the  information they want to receive  including issues they may have a  particular interest in such as scams  internet crime or rural crime they will  also be able to choose whether to  receive this information via email text  or voice message do you have a  brownfield site that you'd like to  promote for development the council has  started work on a new local plan which  will ensure that a plan covering at  least 15 years is in place as part of  this it is important for us to find out  where there are available sites in the  district which may be suitable for  development in the future whether it is  for new homes open space or land for  education or employment use for example  we are therefore calling on those with  an interest in land in the district to  promote their site through the call for  sites we are particularly keen to  identify land that has previously been  developed brownfield which may have  become available since 2011 the  information gathered through the call  for sites will be used to inform the  evidence base to support the new local  plan which will assist us in addressing  national planning policy requirements in  particular meeting housing need the new  local plan however it is at a very early  stage and it is not guaranteed that any  additional land will be required to be  allocated for the development of any use  to find out more on information on the  call for sites or to promote a site  visit w WAW k and follow the call for  sites link under in focus alternatively  contact the planning policy team by  email planning dot policy at Rochford  govt UK or phone 0170 2 3 18 19 1 speak  up on elder abuse helpline and online  reporting form earlier this year saw the  launch of a new elder abuse helpline  powered by Crimestoppers elder abuse is  a national problem it's not specific to  Essex but agencies across the county  felt that it was an issue that needed to  be addressed and have been proactive in  the setting up of this helpline in 2013  to 14 in Essex there are almost 1,500  cases of reported abuse which involved  individuals over the age of 65 the free  24-7 reporting line is anonymous but  callers have the option to leave their  details if they wish and aims to  encourage members of the public to  report any incident of elder abuse  whether it's in a care home hospital or  in the individual's own home cause will  be taken by call agents from the Crime  Stoppers contact centre who have been  trained on how to take calls on elder  abuse this ensures they ask the right  questions to gain as much in  formation as possible the information  will be passed to the relevant local  authorities safeguarding officers if a  criminal offense has taken place  information will also be passed to the  relevant police force and the number for  the reporting line is a 8